00:04:02.920 --> 00:04:04.520
There was one issue,

00:04:05.400 --> 00:04:11.160
and I think it certainly caught me by surprise, I think it caught most of us by surprise,

00:04:11.480 --> 00:04:14.920
that came up at the last meeting and that was the

00:04:15.295 --> 00:04:16.895
driveway entrance

00:04:17.535 --> 00:04:19.055
from 580

00:04:19.055 --> 00:04:20.495
Lake Road onto

00:04:20.735 --> 00:04:21.695
Lake Road.

00:04:22.815 --> 00:04:23.375
And

00:04:25.935 --> 00:04:28.095
I looked at it as

00:04:28.495 --> 00:04:29.215
one

00:04:29.550 --> 00:04:30.350
issue,

00:04:30.350 --> 00:04:32.590
as I was discussing it with

00:04:33.070 --> 00:04:34.750
Agent Halsey, you

00:04:35.150 --> 00:04:38.910
know, he was looking at it as two different issues. So I'd just like to

00:04:39.230 --> 00:04:40.190
clarify

00:04:40.750 --> 00:04:42.190
my understanding

00:04:42.190 --> 00:04:44.590
of the issues out there

00:04:46.905 --> 00:04:48.905
because it would be nice to

00:04:49.625 --> 00:04:51.305
get good resolution

00:04:51.865 --> 00:04:53.945
on the matters here before we

00:04:54.265 --> 00:04:56.025
make a motion to

00:04:56.425 --> 00:04:57.065
act on it.

00:04:58.580 --> 00:05:00.340
The regulation stated

00:05:00.340 --> 00:05:02.900
that there must be a 100 foot separation

00:05:02.900 --> 00:05:04.740
between the two driveways.

00:05:08.820 --> 00:05:10.100
Given that there was not,

00:05:12.015 --> 00:05:17.615
there were also words in the same section, and we'll put them up here in a minute on access control,

00:05:18.335 --> 00:05:20.335
that talked to the benefits

00:05:20.735 --> 00:05:22.175
of common driveways.

00:05:24.460 --> 00:05:27.420
And I understand that neither

00:05:27.980 --> 00:05:28.940
the

00:05:29.580 --> 00:05:31.820
current property owner or

00:05:32.300 --> 00:05:33.500
the potential

00:05:34.620 --> 00:05:37.020
property buyer for the retail store

00:05:37.595 --> 00:05:41.115
are interested in sharing a common driveway.

00:05:41.595 --> 00:05:41.995
It

00:05:43.515 --> 00:05:47.035
was pointed out that the commission does have discretion on using that.

00:05:50.500 --> 00:05:54.900
My interest in bringing that up at the last meeting

00:05:55.780 --> 00:05:57.860
was in an attempt

00:05:57.940 --> 00:05:58.500
to

00:05:58.820 --> 00:06:01.860
provide a condition of approval

00:06:02.525 --> 00:06:05.405
that would allow the application

00:06:06.685 --> 00:06:07.485
to

00:06:09.165 --> 00:06:11.325
meet our regulations.

00:06:14.765 --> 00:06:16.845
That's why I looked at it

00:06:17.565 --> 00:06:18.285
as one

00:06:18.660 --> 00:06:19.460
issue.

00:06:20.820 --> 00:06:21.940
There's two there.

00:06:22.980 --> 00:06:23.460
I

00:06:27.220 --> 00:06:31.540
attended some training that Mark Branch gave our zoning board of appeals

00:06:31.620 --> 00:06:32.740
earlier this year.

00:06:34.895 --> 00:06:37.295
And in that we talked about

00:06:37.615 --> 00:06:38.975
the regulations

00:06:38.975 --> 00:06:40.655
for a town being

00:06:42.175 --> 00:06:43.695
kind of a best

00:06:44.095 --> 00:06:45.055
approach

00:06:45.055 --> 00:06:48.895
cookie cutter thing thinking that all lots were about the same.

00:06:51.320 --> 00:06:52.840
There was a recognition

00:06:53.080 --> 00:06:53.720
that

00:06:56.840 --> 00:06:59.080
all lots are not the same,

00:06:59.560 --> 00:07:02.280
and so there has to be a process for dealing with that.

00:07:07.535 --> 00:07:12.815
That process, as I understand it, is what the zoning board of appeals is all about.

00:07:13.375 --> 00:07:16.335
And they can grant a variance

00:07:16.950 --> 00:07:18.790
when a piece of property

00:07:18.870 --> 00:07:20.550
doesn't seem to meet

00:07:20.790 --> 00:07:24.070
the requirement. I think most people on the commission

00:07:24.470 --> 00:07:27.830
thought the proposed driveway was put in a good place.

00:07:30.645 --> 00:07:34.085
As we had talked at both public hearings

00:07:34.165 --> 00:07:35.445
that we had held,

00:07:37.365 --> 00:07:39.765
we act on the application not

00:07:39.765 --> 00:07:44.565
whether we like it or not, but whether or not it meets our regulations.

00:07:46.990 --> 00:07:48.350
And so I was

00:07:50.430 --> 00:07:51.310
hung up

00:07:51.710 --> 00:07:53.630
and not sure how to go

00:07:54.510 --> 00:07:55.150
with

00:07:55.310 --> 00:07:56.670
the 100 foot

00:07:57.550 --> 00:07:59.470
regulation that we weren't meeting there.

00:08:03.295 --> 00:08:04.335
So that's

00:08:04.895 --> 00:08:06.975
where I think we are tonight.

00:08:09.535 --> 00:08:14.655
I know agent Hallisey asked the applicants if they were interested in

00:08:14.950 --> 00:08:16.070
an extension

00:08:16.230 --> 00:08:18.950
to allow us to try and sort this out.

00:08:21.590 --> 00:08:22.310
Maybe

00:08:22.550 --> 00:08:27.190
at the time it wasn't recognized there was anything to sort out. I still think there might be.

00:08:28.135 --> 00:08:29.895
But we were told that

00:08:30.135 --> 00:08:31.255
the applicants

00:08:31.735 --> 00:08:34.295
were not interested in an extension

00:08:34.375 --> 00:08:35.975
at that point in time.

00:08:37.575 --> 00:08:40.375
So anyhow, what I'd like to do next is

00:08:40.695 --> 00:08:42.535
I'm going to put up on the screen

00:08:46.110 --> 00:08:48.510
section of our regulations on

00:08:49.790 --> 00:08:50.990
access control

00:08:50.990 --> 00:08:52.510
so we can all see

00:08:52.990 --> 00:08:56.910
what the words are that are going to be the

00:08:57.435 --> 00:08:59.675
most of our discussion here this evening.

00:09:00.075 --> 00:09:03.195
So Abby, can you allow me to share my screen?

00:09:03.835 --> 00:09:13.270
>> You should have the ability to. Let me know if you can't. Mr. Chairman, the record Mark Brans, one thing before you to that there is just one thing I would like to comment on if I may.

00:09:14.630 --> 00:09:17.990
Yes go ahead Mark. I did review your record

00:09:18.790 --> 00:09:21.990
the applicant has stated that this will be a retail use

00:09:22.885 --> 00:09:26.645
they have not disclosed the tenant and they do not have to either,

00:09:26.885 --> 00:09:27.925
it is irrelevant.

00:09:28.965 --> 00:09:33.365
Some of the letters that you received from members of the public speculated

00:09:33.365 --> 00:09:36.165
that this would be a particular tenant, a Dollar General,

00:09:37.220 --> 00:09:39.220
and asked you to deny it

00:09:39.540 --> 00:09:41.460
because it was Dollar General.

00:09:42.260 --> 00:09:45.220
I must instruct you to completely disregard

00:09:45.220 --> 00:09:46.740
those kinds of statements.

00:09:48.740 --> 00:09:49.780
Whether it's

00:09:49.860 --> 00:09:51.380
Dollar Tree, Dollar General,

00:09:51.835 --> 00:09:53.435
Aldi, CVS,

00:09:53.435 --> 00:09:56.555
Walgreens, whoever it is, is irrelevant.

00:09:56.635 --> 00:09:59.915
Your regulations talk about a retail use,

00:10:00.155 --> 00:10:02.235
it's a permitted use in the zone,

00:10:02.555 --> 00:10:06.955
and who the tenant is, who the retailer is, is completely irrelevant.

00:10:08.490 --> 00:10:10.010
If you feel you cannot

00:10:10.170 --> 00:10:12.970
disregard that you need to recuse yourselves

00:10:13.130 --> 00:10:18.570
but I would just say to you that who the tenant is has no place in your discussions.

00:10:18.730 --> 00:10:19.050
Thank you.

00:10:22.255 --> 00:10:29.375
>> Okay, thanks Attorney Branch. And that's why I think we tried to make it very clear at both public hearings

00:10:30.015 --> 00:10:30.575
that

00:10:31.295 --> 00:10:34.415
it wasn't whether we were in favor of one particular

00:10:35.240 --> 00:10:39.640
store or another, it was solely based on does the application

00:10:39.960 --> 00:10:41.400
meet the regulations?

00:10:41.400 --> 00:10:44.360
If yes, we have to approve it, if no,

00:10:44.600 --> 00:10:48.280
we have to deny it. And so that's where we are tonight.

00:10:58.355 --> 00:10:59.875
So here's the section

00:11:00.275 --> 00:11:00.995
out

00:11:02.435 --> 00:11:04.115
of our 23.4.

00:11:05.790 --> 00:11:07.470
I am aware that

00:11:10.350 --> 00:11:11.470
there was some

00:11:12.830 --> 00:11:14.990
feedback

00:11:17.975 --> 00:11:18.695
that

00:11:18.855 --> 00:11:19.655
possibly

00:11:21.255 --> 00:11:24.375
Ben Franklin Plumbing and a retail store

00:11:24.535 --> 00:11:26.775
were not similar uses here.

00:11:30.690 --> 00:11:31.570
Certainly,

00:11:33.810 --> 00:11:36.690
I read that, you know, it looks like

00:11:39.730 --> 00:11:44.770
the comma is around paths and sidewalks for similar use. Don't know exactly

00:11:44.930 --> 00:11:46.290
if that

00:11:46.325 --> 00:11:47.045
jimmy:

00:11:47.285 --> 00:11:48.085
requires

00:11:48.405 --> 00:11:53.685
you know if similar uses makes a difference with respect to common driveway

00:11:53.765 --> 00:11:54.805
